    "body": "Fixes #8158\n\nSince #7489, `setup_test_directory()` adds `CYTHON_REFNANNY` to `CDEFS`, but it only runs in the main process. The worker processes of `runtests.py -jN` only inherit `CDEFS` if they are forked, so with `forkserver` (the default on Linux since Python 3.14) and `spawn` (macOS, Windows) they compiled all tests without refnanny. CI runs `-j7`, so its Linux jobs on 3.14 and later and all macOS and Windows jobs have had no reference count checks since February. The issue has a reproducer, and a known leak (#8156) that passes because of this.\n\n- `runtests()` adds the define again, as it did before #7489: it runs in every test process. `setup_test_directory()` still builds the refnanny module once, and the workers find it through `sys.path`, which `spawn` and `forkserver` pass on.\n- The `--debug-*` options were lost in the workers too. They are now options of the argument parser, which collects them in `options.debug_flags`. `main()` sets them right after parsing, before anything imports the compiler modules, which read some of them at import time, and `runtests_callback()` sets them again in the worker processes.\n- `tests/run/refnanny_enabled.pyx` checks that it was compiled with `CYTHON_REFNANNY`. Its new `refnanny` tag excludes it when `runtests.py` runs without refnanny (`--no-refnanny`, PyPy, GraalPy). On master it fails with `-j2` on 3.14 and passes with `-j1`.\n\nI didn't force the `fork` start method instead: Windows doesn't have it, it isn't safe on macOS, and it would fork a multi-threaded process here, since `ProcessPoolExecutor` starts the workers on the first `submit()`, when the time stamper thread is already running.\n\nTested on Linux with GitHub's CPython builds and the CFLAGS of `Tools/ci-run.sh`:\n- `refnanny_enabled` passes with `-j1` and `-j2` on 3.13t, 3.14, 3.14t, 3.15 and 3.15t, and `--no-refnanny` skips it. The `break` leak of #8156 is reported again with `-j2`.\n- `--debug-trace-code-generation` now writes the same trace with `-j2` as with `-j1` (24 comments in the C file of a small test, none with `-j2` before).\n- With refnanny active in the workers, refnanny reports no errors in the existing tests: the full suite (C and C++) on 3.14 (23,041 tests) and 3.14t (23,037 tests), 3.14 with `-DCYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE=1` and with `--limited-api` (C and C++), and 3.15 and 3.15t (C). So this shouldn't turn the Linux jobs red. I couldn't test macOS and Windows.\n- The only failures in these runs have other causes. `embed_modules` and `EmbedTest` can't find libpython here because the `LIBDIR` of GitHub's builds is under `/opt/hostedtoolcache`; with the builds mounted there, as on the runners, they pass. In the `--limited-api` run, `common_utility_types` failed because I hadn't built Cython with `--cython-limited-api` as CI does: the refnanny module then registers a second `_cython_*` module (the same happens on master with `-j1`). With that build, it passes.\n- `runcodestyle.py` and codespell.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01GwUvhmzgfkiZ6vo4uGyesN\n",
