            "commit": {
                "author": {
                    "date": "2026-11-24T21:33:42Z",
                    "email": "pylaterreur@gmail.com",
                    "name": "Pierre-Yves Le Borgne"
                },
                "comment_count": 0,
                "committer": {
                    "date": "2026-11-24T23:48:53Z",
                    "email": "pylaterreur@gmail.com",
                    "name": "Pierre-Yves Le Borgne"
                },
                "message": "Test runner: Enable refnanny in the worker processes of parallel runs\n\nSince GH-7489, setup_test_directory() adds the CYTHON_REFNANNY define to\nCDEFS, but it only runs in the main process.  The worker processes of a\nparallel test run (-jN) only inherit CDEFS if they are forked, so with\nthe \"forkserver\" start method (the default on Linux since Python 3.14)\nand with \"spawn\" (macOS, Windows), they compiled all tests without\nrefnanny.  Add the define in runtests() again, which runs in each test\nprocess, and keep building the refnanny module once in\nsetup_test_directory().\n\nThe --debug-* options of runtests.py were lost in the worker processes\nin the same way: pass them on in the options and set them again in\nconfigure_cython().\n\nAdd a test that fails if runtests.py compiles the tests without\nCYTHON_REFNANNY while reference count checking is enabled.  The new\n\"refnanny\" tag excludes it otherwise (--no-refnanny, PyPy, GraalPy).\n\nFixes #8158\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GwUvhmzgfkiZ6vo4uGyesN",
