                "message": "Test runner: Declare the --debug-* options in the argument parser\n\nInstead of taking the --debug-* flags out of sys.argv before parsing the\nother options, declare an option for each flag in DebugFlags, which\nappends the flag name to \"options.debug_flags\".  The flags now behave\nlike the other options: they can be abbreviated and cannot go between\ntwo test selectors.  The underscore spelling that the old filter also\naccepted (--debug_trace_code_generation) is gone, as in the cython\ncommand line.\n\nmain() sets the flags right after parsing, before anything imports the\ncompiler modules, since some flags are only read at import time\n(debug_trace_code_generation in Nodes.py, debug_disposal_code and\ndebug_coercion in ExprNodes.py) and setup_test_directory() imports the\ncompiler in the main process when it builds the refnanny module with\npyximport.  runtests_callback() sets them again in the worker processes\nof parallel runs, which only inherit them from the main process if they\nare forked.  configure_cython() no longer needs to set them.\n\nThe CYTHON_REFNANNY define is added in runtests() and not in\nsetup_test_directory() because runtests() runs in each test process,\nwhile setup_test_directory() only runs in the main process.  The worker\nprocesses of a parallel run (-jN) only inherit the CDEFS of the main\nprocess if they are forked, and the default start method is \"forkserver\"\non Linux since Python 3.14 and \"spawn\" on macOS and Windows.  Replace\nthe comment at the define, which described where it used to be, with\none that says why it is set there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GwUvhmzgfkiZ6vo4uGyesN",
